An edge carrying a `script` hook runs it and reports `script {name}: ok` after the status line. The
fixture script is written by the case but `pytest-txtar` cannot express its mode, so the first `cmd`
line chmods it — see README. The script's side effect lands in the workdir and is asserted through
`expected/`.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the note is written
            hooks: ["script note"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/note --
#!/bin/sh
echo "playbook" >> "$BOOPING_WORKDIR/note.log"
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- cmd --
chmod +x ../home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/note
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks intaking --workdir run
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks noted --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created index.md
not-started → intaking
frontmatter: status=intaking
intaking → noted
frontmatter: status=noted
script note: ok
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/note.log --
playbook
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: noted
---
